                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "68abed55-8d26-3eef-9b7d-e07ae100cea4",
                        "entry_id": "77635899-edb1-349b-a83b-899383e3ced1",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To eject again."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "f3c545c9-8093-4d5d-997e-ba3290fc19d3",
                                "sense_id": "68abed55-8d26-3eef-9b7d-e07ae100cea4",
                                "text": "An average fission product originating in the collected material was found to reeject about 10,000 atoms, whereas one originating in the emitter reejected only about 1000 atoms."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "73cec5ff-7ce3-489c-ae1e-e08cfee0ec44",
                                "sense_id": "68abed55-8d26-3eef-9b7d-e07ae100cea4",
                                "text": "Moreover, to maintain a normal output, the ventricles have to continually reeject the regurgitated blood and are in a situation not unlike a person desperately trying to bale water out of a rapidly leaking boat."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "4bbd9360-1ad6-4ffa-afb2-e0c639a87842",
                                "sense_id": "68abed55-8d26-3eef-9b7d-e07ae100cea4",
                                "text": "...whereas nuclear power is used to reeject matter at higher than SN velocities through the BLR, NLR, and galactic halo, enriching the IGM with metals."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
